  "titleText": {
    "es": "Temístocles dijo que su hijo pequeño gobernaba toda Grecia: «Atenas gobierna toda Grecia; yo controlo Atenas; mi mujer me controla; y mi hijo pequeño la controla a ella.» Por tanto, hoy en día el mundo está controlado por los que emiten anuncios en Dora la Exploradora.",
    "en": "Themistocles said his infant son ruled all Greece -- \"Athens rules all Greece; I control Athens; my wife controls me; and my infant son controls her.\" Thus, nowadays the world is controlled by whoever buys advertising time on Dora the Explorer.",
    "noteEn": "The Spanish and English texts are the exact title attributes from the Spanish archive and official xkcd. OCR dropped the accents in INSTALÓ and BOTÓN and misread the initial letters of UNIFICADOS and the final EEUU abbreviation. The chart boxes, connecting lines, arrows, and dotted bypass line are structural artwork; EEUU is an audited abbreviation exclusion."
  },
